\title{zuid: Universally Unique Identifiers, Their Encodings and Their Kin}
\description{
Parses, validates, inspects and generates universally unique identifiers (UUIDs) of every version defined by RFC 9562 \doi{10.17487/RFC9562}, and re-encodes them in alternative text forms such as Crockford base32, base36, base58, base62, base64url, Proquint and Niceware words. The same functions read the fields and creation time of related identifier formats: Universally Unique Lexicographically Sortable Identifiers (ULID), TypeID, UPID, SCRU128 and SCRU64 (Sortable, Clock and Random number-based Unique identifiers), K-Sortable Unique Identifiers (KSUID), Snowflake, XID, 'MongoDB' ObjectId, NanoID, Cuid2, Sqids and content identifiers (CID). Detection never assumes a format that the input does not prove. Identifiers are generated from the operating system's entropy source, never from R's random number generator. No other package is needed at run time.
}
